  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, acc=0.639) uses PCA n2000 as the RNA encoder within a multimodal multi-profile avgpool weighted-fusion setup. RNA is the dominant signal (RNA-only 0.591 vs image-only 0.208), yet we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA, a simple linear projection). This leaves major uncertainty about whether a learned nonlinear embedding could substantially improve the RNA branch. Question: Does scvi_n200 (a learned nonlinear latent embedding) outperform PCA n2000 in the best multimodal configuration? Config_031 changes only the RNA encoder relative to config_019, making it a clean single-variable comparison. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly probes the highest-impact untested design axis (RNA encoder quality) within the already-validated best architecture, so a positive result immediately yields a new best configuration, while a negative result rules out scvi and focuses remaining budget on scgpt or the image encoder. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

